jobs.description:
As a Warehouse Planner, you are responsible for planning, coordinating and monitoring daily warehouse operations. You will analyze workloads, staffing requirements and operational priorities to ensure all activities are completed efficiently and on time.

Your responsibilities include:

- Planning and coordinating daily warehouse activities;
- Releasing work orders in line with operational priorities;
- Analyzing orders, inventory levels and workforce requirements;
- Monitoring operational performance and identifying bottlenecks;
- Solving planning issues and implementing effective solutions;
- Preparing reports and recommending process improvements;
- Communicating with customers, carriers and suppliers;
- Supporting inventory and location management activities when required;
- Contributing to continuous improvement initiatives within the warehouse operation. [Warehouse...er 2 AH213 | PDF]

Working hours are based on a two-shift schedule:

- 06:00 - 14:30
- 13:30 - 22:00

Depending on operational demands, the afternoon shift may occasionally be extended until 00:00.

We are looking for someone who enjoys taking responsibility and thrives in a dynamic environment.

You have:

- MBO working and thinking level or equivalent;
- An interest in logistics and warehouse operations;
- Strong organizational and planning skills;
- Good communication skills;
- Fluent English skills, both spoken and written;
- Dutch language skills are a strong advantage, but not required;
- Customer service experience is beneficial but not mandatory;
- A proactive and professional attitude;
- The ability to work effectively under pressure;
- A strong willingness to learn and develop both personally and professionally.

As an Industrial Cleaning Specialist, your primary responsibility is to clean and prepare returned packaging materials for reuse. This includes removing stickers, barcodes, and labels, as well as occasionally disassembling and reassembling products. The job is both physically active and varied, offering you new challenges every day. If you thrive on being hands-on and enjoy an active role, this is the perfect opportunity for you.

Your key tasks include:

- Cleaning formwork and other packaging materials;
- Removing stickers, barcodes, and labels without damaging surfaces;
- Disassembling and reassembling products as needed.

You’ll work in two shifts: early (06:00–15:00) and late (15:00–00:00), ensuring flexibility and variety in your schedule.

- Proficiency in English;
- Physical fitness and ability to perform active work throughout the day;
- Availability for two-shift work without exceptions.

As an Order Picker, you help make sure customers receive their orders quickly and correctly.

Your tasks include:

- Picking orders using a handheld scanner;
- Checking products and quantities;
- Packing and preparing orders for shipment;
- Placing products in the correct warehouse locations;
- Loading and unloading trucks;
- Helping colleagues when needed;
- Keeping the warehouse clean and safe.

Working Hours

You will work 40 hours per week.

You can choose between:

Morning Shift

- 07:00 AM to 04:00 PM

Evening Shift

- 04:00 PM to 01:00 AM

- MBO level or similar working and thinking level;
- Motivated and willing to work hard;
- Accurate and reliable;
- Able to speak Dutch or English;
- Physically fit and comfortable with warehouse work;
- Own transportation (car, scooter, moped, or e-bike);
- Warehouse experience is a plus, but not required.
